close_reason: "Fixed in PR #1779: the recovery-command shell dialect is declared with PM_COMMAND_SHELL, and the powershell form renders single-quoted literals that never expand"
contract_change:
  api: "Rendered recovery commands (suggested_retry, restore_with, next steps) and the SDK quoteCommandArg / renderPmCommand"
  before: "Windows recovery commands were always CommandLineToArgvW double-quoted, so PowerShell expanded $, $(...) and backticks; the intent restore_with and the git rm --cached remediation always used POSIX single quotes"
  after: "PM_COMMAND_SHELL declares posix, cmd or powershell (default cmd on Windows, posix elsewhere); powershell renders single-quoted literals; every rendered command, including the intent restore_with and the git remediation, follows the declared dialect"
  migrate: Set PM_COMMAND_SHELL=powershell (or pwsh) when pasting pm recovery commands into PowerShell; SDK callers can pass a CommandShellDialect as the third argument of quoteCommandArg and renderPmCommand
escape_class: production_defect
